            <ArticleTitle>Vasospasm in a coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery aneurysms are not believed to have enough intact smooth muscle to generate significant vasoconstriction. A case is presented illustrating vasospasm of a large fusiform aneurysm of a right coronary artery during angioplasty. Pathophysiology of aneurysms is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
